  "notes": {
    "migration": "OpenAI removes these models from the API on 2026-10-23: gpt-3.5-turbo-0125, gpt-3.5-turbo, gpt-3.5-turbo-completions, gpt-4-0613, gpt-4, gpt-4-0613-completions, gpt-4-completions, gpt-4-1106-preview, gpt-4-turbo, gpt-4-turbo-2024-04-09, gpt-4-turbo-completions, gpt-4.1-nano, gpt-4.1-nano-2025-04-14, gpt-4o-2024-05-13, gpt-image-1, o1-2024-12-17, o1, o1-pro-2025-03-19, o1-pro, o3-mini-2025-01-31, o3-mini, o4-mini-2025-04-16, o4-mini. Calls that name them fail after that date. Recommended replacements: gpt-3.5-turbo-0125 to gpt-5.6-terra; gpt-4-0613 to gpt-5.6-sol; gpt-4-1106-preview to gpt-5.6-sol; gpt-4-turbo to gpt-5.6-sol; gpt-4.1-nano to gpt-5.6-luna; gpt-4o-2024-05-13 to gpt-5.6-sol; gpt-image-1 to gpt-image-2.5-sunburst or gpt-image-2.5-flare; o1-2024-12-17 to gpt-5.6-sol; o1-pro-2025-03-19 to gpt-5.6-sol (reasoning.mode: pro); o3-mini-2025-01-31 to gpt-5.6-sol; o4-mini-2025-04-16 to gpt-5.6-terra. A newer model can answer differently, so test the switch rather than only renaming.",
    "edgeCases": [
      "A model name read from an environment variable, a config file or a variable set elsewhere is not found.",
      "Fine-tuned models built on these, whose ids start with ft:, are not matched.",
      "A model key nested inside another option of the call, such as metadata, is reported too.",
      "Not found: a quoted \"model\" key, template strings, Python f-strings or **kwargs, and calls made through other libraries such as LangChain or Vercel's SDK.",
      "A mocked API response that names the model, such as an msw or nock handler for the endpoint, is reported too.",
      "Azure OpenAI calls are reported too, though Azure names deployments its own way and sets its own retirement dates."
    ]
  },
